counterfactuals.output:
A computer-implemented method for dental visualization, comprising:

receiving one or more facial data records representing at least a portion of a patient’s face;

automatically detecting, in the one or more facial data records, a mouth region of the patient;

determining an orientation of the patient’s face based on the one or more facial data records;

providing a virtual tooth data record representing at least one virtual tooth or a proposed dental restoration; and

positioning the virtual tooth data record relative to the detected mouth region based at least in part on the determined orientation of the patient’s face, thereby generating a visualization of the at least one virtual tooth or proposed dental restoration in relation to the patient’s face.
